.TH AUTHD 8 "September 2026" "authd" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
authd \- Peios PGSS Logon authority
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/sbin/authd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B authd
is the Peios authentication authority.  It accepts logon requests on
.IR /run/logon.sock ,
coordinates credential verification with registered principal sources on
.IR /run/psi.sock ,
and returns a KACS primary token and profile for an authenticated principal.
Identity queries are served separately on
.IR /run/ident.sock .
.PP
The daemon does not verify credentials or launch sessions.  Principal sources
such as
.BR lpsd (8)
verify credentials, and clients such as
.BR login (1)
install granted tokens on themselves.
.PP
The service is normally started by peinit from the registry definition shipped
in
.IR /usr/share/regim/authd-service.reg .
It takes no command-line options.
.SH SECURITY
.B authd
runs at PeiosTcb integrity with SeCreateTokenPrivilege and SeTcbPrivilege.
Its executable must carry a valid Peios TCB PIP signature.  Machine logon
policy is read from
.IR Machine\eGeneric\eAuthn\ePolicy .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/logon.sock
PGSS Logon client socket.
.TP
.I /run/psi.sock
Principal Source Interface registration socket.
.TP
.I /run/ident.sock
Identity lookup socket.
.TP
.I /usr/share/regim/authd-policy.reg
Default machine authentication-policy seed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR login (1),
.BR lps (1),
.BR lpsd (8)
